Build instructions for Windows without Cygwin
---------------------------------------------

Requirements
------------
  * Visual Studio (Community or similar)
    - Previously was Visual Studio Express
  * libxml binary libraries
    - Libs:
      . libxml2-2.7.8.win32
      . iconv-1.9.2.win32
      . zlib-1.2.5
    - From: https://www.zlatkovic.com/libxml.en.html
    - Compiled with the /MD Option (Multi-threaded DLL)
      - Therefore the program needs to be compiled with the same option
  * Inno Setup (For building Distributions)
    - Using 

Building
--------
From the base directory (with aux and HISTORY files), run

  A:\>%cd%\win\build_win.bat

This will create:

  - sac-102.0-win32.exe     Self-extracing Installer
  - Release                 Directory where the sac build resides

The errors and warnings will be collected into errors.txt and warnings.txt

Cleaning
--------
From the base directory (with aux and HISTORY files), run

  A:\>%cd%\win\build_win.bat

Versions
--------

  - MSBuild    - C:\Program Files\MSBuild\12.0\Bin\MSBuild.exe
  - Inno Setup - C:\Program Files\Inno Setup 5\ISCC
  - Visual Studio with a working C++ compiler